  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Private-Delivered Metro Sao Paulo Line 4 Phase III Extension</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Line 4 extension to Tabo&#xe3;o da Serra is a groundbreaking project for Metro S&#xe3;o Paulo as it marks the first expansion beyond S&#xe3;o Paulo city boundaries. The project includes 3.3 kilometers of new underground tracks and two new stations to be implemented and operated by a private concessionaire through an ongoing Public-Private Partnership. Activities financed by the project includes: Civil Works, Power Electric Supply, Telecommunications, Auxiliary (safety and operational equipment such as escalators, elevators, ventilation, emergency lighting, and platform doors, along with comprehensive passenger control and monitoring systems), signaling, supervision and capacity building. The Project aims to improve commutes by providing a quicker, more efficient public transport option, thereby reducing travel time, encouraging a shift from private cars and diesel buses, and reducing greenhouse gas emissions.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Development Objectives (PDO) are to improve low-carbon mobility, increase job accessibility in Metro Line 4&apos;s Catchment Area, and strengthen public sector capacity to structure and manage private-sector participation in urban transport.</narrative>
  </description>
